{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>My soul loathes it:</b> whether I have refrained so as not to speak, or I have spoken — as in the matter of 'I held my peace'; I wearied myself with my roar." "<b>I will abandon it:</b> some say it is from עזוב תעזוב (abandon, you shall abandon). The one closer to me: it is as it sounds."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:17.026028711Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}